From: Claude Code (no-visible-windows fix round, 2026-10-12) on behalf of dmmdea
Subject: [PATCH 0006] hide the companion CLI's console window on Windows

cobratree.RunCLICommand (generated shellout.go) started the companion CLI with a bare
exec.CommandContext. It runs once per Cobra-mirror MCP tool call, in a server its host starts
without a console; a console program started that way gets a NEW visible console window on
Windows (a Windows Terminal window on the operator's desktop). The command is now built by
newCLICommand, which hides it (CREATE_NO_WINDOW + SW_HIDE) through the package's hideWindow.
New files: hide_windows.go, hide_other.go, hide_windows_test.go. The test helper that builds the
argv-echo binary is hidden the same way.
---
diff --git a/internal/mcp/cobratree/hide_other.go b/internal/mcp/cobratree/hide_other.go
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..cd573d73
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/mcp/cobratree/hide_other.go
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
